<section class="fa-ppc-block"><p class="eyebrow">Proof without vanity metrics</p><h2>What a Useful Paid-Search Report Should Prove</h2><p>I do not publish invented advisor results or anonymous AUM claims. When a firm approves a case study, proof should connect spend to qualified consultations and suitable opportunities—not stop at platform conversions.</p><div class="fa-ppc-evidence-grid"><div><small>01 · Demand</small><strong>Search term → service</strong><p>Which queries reflect an actual planning need?</p></div><div><small>02 · Qualification</small><strong>Lead → suitable prospect</strong><p>Which inquiries match the firm’s approved criteria?</p></div><div><small>03 · Meeting</small><strong>Booked → attended</strong><p>Where do confirmation and follow-up break down?</p></div><div><small>04 · Outcome</small><strong>Opportunity → relationship</strong><p>Which campaigns contribute to appropriate growth?</p></div></div><div class="fa-ppc-inline-cta"><div><strong>Bring your current numbers.</strong><span>We can map the missing steps between click, lead, meeting, and opportunity.</span></div><a class="pe-button pe-button-primary" href="${BOOKING}">Review the account →</a></div></section>
